<title>JORDAN: Jordan dinar overnight rates drop to 5.1 pct.</title>
<headline>Jordan dinar overnight rates drop to 5.1 pct.</headline>
<dateline>AMMAN 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The weighted average overnight interbank rate on the Jordanian dinar fell to 5.1 percent on Wednesday after a week-long holiday, the central bank said.</p>
<p>It said five banks traded on the market in 10 reported transactions with a total value of 13.6 million dinars ($19 million).</p>
<p>Rates fluctuated in a wide 6.00-8.00 pct band last Thursday, the last working day before the Moslem Eid al Fitr holiday, which ended on Wednesday.</p>
<p>$1 = 0.7080 dinar</p>
<p>-- Amman newsroom +962 6 623 776</p>
